1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:06,700
Meet Ordo, the AI maintenance engineer for your codebase, built on IBM watsonx dot AI.

2
00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:26,100
Technical debt grows quietly. It piles up unseen, until it becomes an outage, slow delivery, or a security incident. Today's scanners produce long, noisy reports, ranked by rule severity, with no business context and no fix path. So the list gets ignored.

3
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:41,500
Ordo closes that gap in one pass. It analyzes a GitHub repository, ranks every finding by real risk, turns the list into a roadmap, and prepares the fix, the tests, and the pull request.

4
00:00:43,700 --> 00:00:55,170
The ranking is done by IBM Granite on watsonx dot AI. Every finding gets an urgency, business impact, and fix effort score, plus a plain English reason. Let's see it live.

5
00:00:57,167 --> 00:01:02,937
This is Ordo's web app, running on Vercel. We'll scan a real project, Agora, straight from GitHub.

6
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:16,580
I click Scan Repo Now and paste the repository link. While Bob streams the scan, Ordo reads the code through the GitHub API and runs five debt detectors.

7
00:01:20,767 --> 00:01:31,587
Seconds later, the dashboard. Twenty findings, nineteen of them high urgency, each scored by the Granite model for urgency, impact, and effort, with its reasoning attached.

8
00:01:36,533 --> 00:01:44,363
The overview breaks the debt down by category, shows repository stats, including zero test files, and lists the top issues.

9
00:01:45,567 --> 00:01:51,877
The roadmap is written by the model too. An overall assessment, then three phases the team can schedule.

10
00:01:54,100 --> 00:02:01,440
Open any issue to drill in. Ask why it is ranked here, and watsonx explains its reasoning in plain English.

11
00:02:02,467 --> 00:02:14,157
Then generate the fix. Ordo returns a step by step remediation plan, code hints, a testing strategy, and a pull request summary, ready to copy straight into GitHub with one click.

12
00:02:18,200 --> 00:02:33,810
The same engine runs inside IBM Bob, IBM's AI coding assistant. Ordo ships as a custom Bob mode with three skills, analyze repo, explain issue, and generate fix, so developers can do all of this from chat.

13
00:02:34,700 --> 00:02:37,970
And the full pitch deck is one click away, under Docs.

14
00:02:40,900 --> 00:02:46,200
Ordo turns software chaos into order. Try it today at ordowithbob.vercel.app.

